            <ArticleTitle>Sutureless extraocular muscle biopsy technique.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>614-616</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5301/ejo.5000933</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To describe a simple and novel technique of obtaining an extraocular muscle (EOM) biopsy.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Our sutureless method involves obtaining a full-thickness 3-mm EOM specimen using a disposable punch biopsy.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The procedure was performed successfully, with no worsening of eye movement, muscle weakness, or cosmetic defects postoperatively. The acquired full-thickness specimen was sufficient for analysis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">This technique to obtain an EOM biopsy allows a straightforward sutureless method, providing an adequate sample for tissue scrutiny.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
